  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday through Sunday)\nIssued at 1213 AM CDT Mon Jul 20 2026\n\nUpper level ridge to build south across the Southern Plains and\nbring hot and dry conditions for much of the upcoming week for\nWest Central Texas. Hottest readings will likely be across the Big\nCountry closest to the ridge, where temperatures will climb above\nthe 100 degree mark. Will likely be a few degrees cooler to the\nsouth, both farther from the ridge and where they will still have\nwet soils from the recent heavy rainfall. \n\nDoes look like surface dewpoints will be low enough that heat\nindex values will stay below advisory criteria for now, but actual\ntemperatures across the Big Country may begin to inch towards the\n105 degree criteria by mid week. A future Heat Advisory may end \nup being needed.\n\nWill also keep an eye on the tropical system in the Gulf. Too many\nunknowns to do much with it now, but will continue to monitor.",
